{
  "id": "ep217",
  "duration": 55.216,
  "beats": [
    {
      "start": 0.08,
      "end": 5.152,
      "text": "A spacecraft once found strange, linear scars carved into a deep-space rock.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "951 Gaspra.jpg",
        "credit": "NASA",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:951_Gaspra.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 0.0,
          "end": 5.167,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 5.152,
      "end": 14.272,
      "text": "In 1991, [NASA\u2019s](/n\u02c8\u00e6s\u02c8\u00e6s/) Galileo spacecraft approached the asteroid 951 [Gaspra](/\u0261\u02c8\u00e6sp\u0279\u02c8\u0251/) while traveling toward Jupiter.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Galileo spacecraft in the KSC SAEF-2 facility (KSC-89PC-0698).jpg",
        "credit": "NASA",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Galileo_spacecraft_in_the_KSC_SAEF-2_facility_(KSC-89PC-0698).jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 5.167,
          "end": 9.733,
          "kind": "cover",
          "motion": "camera"
        },
        {
          "start": 9.733,
          "end": 14.267,
          "kind": "detail",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 14.272,
      "end": 21.267,
      "text": "Since its discovery in 1916, astronomers saw [Gaspra](/\u0261\u02c8\u00e6sp\u0279\u02c8\u0251/) as nothing more than a tiny point of light.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "designed card"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 14.267,
          "end": 21.267,
          "kind": "designed",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 21.267,
      "end": 27.987,
      "text": "Galileo closed the gap, snapping fifty-seven images from as close as 3,300 miles away.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "PIA00079.jpg",
        "credit": "NASA/JPL",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:PIA00079.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 21.267,
          "end": 28.0,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 27.987,
      "end": 35.582,
      "text": "The resolution revealed details just 54 meters wide, showing a jagged world lacking large impact craters.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "PIA00118.jpg",
        "credit": "NASA/JPL",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:PIA00118.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 28.0,
          "end": 35.567,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 35.582,
      "end": 42.357,
      "text": "But the biggest shock was the linear grooves, which had previously only been seen on the Martian moon Phobos.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Gaspra Deimos and Phobos.jpg",
        "credit": "NASA",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Gaspra_Deimos_and_Phobos.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 35.567,
          "end": 42.367,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 42.357,
      "end": 50.002,
      "text": "These fractures suggest [Gaspra](/\u0261\u02c8\u00e6sp\u0279\u02c8\u028c/) was born from the violent, catastrophic breakup of a much larger parent asteroid.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Gaspra Deimos and Phobos.jpg",
        "credit": "NASA",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Gaspra_Deimos_and_Phobos.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 42.367,
          "end": 50.0,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 50.002,
      "end": 54.866,
      "text": "It was the first time humanity saw the scars carved into a deep-space rock.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "951 Gaspra.jpg",
        "credit": "NASA",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:951_Gaspra.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 50.0,
          "end": 55.2,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
